8.text:
For the just identified model
$y=Y\beta+u$, $Y=Z\pi+v$ with one instrument $Z$ put
$\delta^{2}=n\pi^{2}{\rm Var}(Z)/\sigma_{v}^{2}$ for the concentration
parameter.  With homoskedastic normal errors, up to $o_{p}(1)$

\begin{equation*}
t_{\pi}=\frac{\hat\pi}{s.e.(\hat\pi)}\;\xrightarrow{d}\;N(\delta,1),
\qquad F=t_{\pi}^{2},
\end{equation*}
so that under the Nagar first order expansion

\begin{equation*}
{\rm Bias}\bigl(\hat\beta_{2SLS}\bigr)\approx
\frac{\sigma_{uv}}{\sigma_{v}^{2}}\;\frac{1}{\delta^{2}}\;, 
\qquad 
{\rm Bias}\bigl(\hat\beta_{OLS}\bigr)\approx\frac{\sigma_{uv}}{\sigma_{v}^{2}} ,
\end{equation*}
and
\begin{equation*}
\rho_{N}\equiv\frac{|{\rm Bias}(\hat\beta_{2SLS})|}
                 {|{\rm Bias}(\hat\beta_{OLS})|}
      \;\approx\;\frac{1}{\delta^{2}} .
\end{equation*}
In particular $\rho_{N}\approx 1/F$ in the first order.  Put
$\delta_{0}^{2}=1/\rho_{0}$ .  For the 10\% relative bias target
$\rho_{0}=0.10$ we want $\delta_{0}=\sqrt{10}$.

For a one–sided $95\%$ lower confidence bound

\begin{equation*}
\hat\delta_{L}=t_{F}-\;z_{0.95},\qquad z_{0.95}=1.645,
\end{equation*}
so that ${\rm P}\{\delta\ge \hat\delta_{L}\}=0.95$.  We require
$\hat\delta_{L}\ge\delta_{0}$, i.e.

\begin{equation*}
t_{F}\ge \delta_{0}+z_{0.95},
\qquad 
F_{\min}\approx\bigl(\delta_{0}+z_{0.95}\bigr)^{2}.
\end{equation*}

With $\delta_{0}=\sqrt{0.10^{-1}}=\sqrt{10}=3.16$

\begin{equation*}
F_{\min}\approx\bigl(\sqrt{10}+1.64\!-\!1.65\bigr)^{2}
        \approx\bigl(3.16+1.645\bigr)^{2}\approx 23\!-\!24,
\end{equation*}
i.e. $F\gtrsim 23$ on the observed first stage gives a $95\%$ one-sided
lower bound for the concentration parameter $\delta^{2}>10$ and hence
${\rm E}\rho_{N}\lesssim0.10$.  In the Stock–Yogo tables this is the
$10\%$ maximal relative bias critical value $F_{1,1}^{0.10}\simeq23.1$.
With the conventional two–sided $1.96$ normal quantile this is
$F\approx (\sqrt{10}+1.96)^{2}\approx26$, the familiar $F>10$ rule of
thumb being the point estimate $ \hat\rho_{N}\approx1/F$.  The size-
distortion $10\%$ critical value is $F\approx16.38$.

